# The `ollama create` recipe for the reader — JoyCaption Beta One, the Q4_K
# quantisation paired with its SigLIP2 vision projector. Stage ① of every tracked
# flow calls the model this file builds, for the prose and for the hosted tags.
#
# Committed because it was never in the repository and cannot be reconstructed
# from it: the two-`FROM` projector pairing is undocumented in Ollama's own
# import and modelfile docs, and the model is a machine-local alias rather than a
# registry tag. Recovered from the operator's live model on 2026-09-19 with
#   ollama show --modelfile joycaption-beta-one-q4k
# and cross-checked against the prototype's own `models/joycaption/Modelfile`.
#
# ── the two artifacts, which this repository does not carry ────────────────────
# `models/` is gitignored; fetch both from
#   https://huggingface.co/concedo/llama-joycaption-beta-one-hf-llava-mmproj-gguf
#   at revision acfe6bf78ae4e411cd5c7c8f4a71ba01f26a5b97
# into `models/joycaption/`, and verify the bytes:
#
#   e8ae55dd07e61d541ab741d6ed63e7810192cea65d7ef8cda69b2a99fb06dc15  4920735936
#     Llama-Joycaption-Beta-One-Hf-Llava-Q4_K.gguf
#   94002cb5c354c7c9e538e64f37d593db9eceeca2e94573bae6cd3b2bd8bb1952   877771808
#     llama-joycaption-beta-one-llava-mmproj-model-f16.gguf
#
# **That repository is the only requantisation that ships the projector.** The
# two most-cited alternatives contain no `mmproj` at all, and the source repo's
# own README misnames the projector as `…-Llava-F16.gguf`, which is the 16 GB
# full-precision *text* model — pairing by that instruction gives a 21 GB
# download and no vision. A model without its projector loads, answers fluently
# and cannot see the photograph, and the failure is silent: after creating it,
# check `ollama show` lists `vision` under Capabilities **and** prints a
# Projector block.
#
# ── the one command, from the repository root ─────────────────────────────────
#
#   ollama create joycaption-beta-one-q4k -f scripts/joycaption.Modelfile
#
# It builds the reader, stage ①, and the same alias answers the hosted tagger —
# which is why TEMPLATE below matters: two calls to one model must not arrive
# framed differently. There was a second command here, `ollama pull qwen3:8b`,
# fetching the sorter for stage ②. Nothing has called it since v0.21 filled the
# sheet from the tagger instead, and v0.22 removed the key that named it.
#
# ── why the TEMPLATE line is here when the original did not carry one ─────────
# The quantisation ships no chat template, so Ollama defaults to passing the
# prompt through verbatim — which `ollama show --modelfile` renders as the line
# below. The prototype relied on that default and its measured captions were
# produced under it, so it is load-bearing. Stating it explicitly pins the
# behaviour to this file instead of to a version of Ollama.
#
# Order matters: the quantisation first, the projector second.

FROM ../models/joycaption/Llama-Joycaption-Beta-One-Hf-Llava-Q4_K.gguf
FROM ../models/joycaption/llama-joycaption-beta-one-llava-mmproj-model-f16.gguf
TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}
